To hash a 24-bit integer, you can use a simple bitwise operation to create a hash. The following function shifts the integer and applies an XOR operation to generate a hash value:

```javascript
function hash24bit(num) {
  return (num << 8) ^ num;
}
```

This function takes a 24-bit integer and returns a hashed value by shifting the bits and combining them with an XOR operation.
